(3.1 Key Clinical Pearls) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.22 0.26 0.32 rg
40 666 Td
(1. Always confirm two independent patient identifiers before administering any blood component.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.22 0.26 0.32 rg
40 648 Td
(2. O Negative uncrossmatched red blood cells should be reserved for catastrophic exsanguinating hemorrhage.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.22 0.26 0.32 rg
40 630 Td
(3. RhD negative women of childbearing age must strictly receive RhD negative components to prevent isoimmunization.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.22 0.26 0.32 rg
40 612 Td
(4. Post-transfusion hemoglobin typically increments by approximately 1 g/dL per unit of packed red cells.) Tj
ET
BT
